{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"6f5e24e1b2268edeef4cca4da912a38f754be7a8"},"timestamp":1547605737,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzOTk2MjA1MjY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3123","origin":"github"},"title":"datalad install subdataset over SSH hops (ssh alias capitalization ignored)","message":"#### What is the problem?\nCandidate source URL is invalid and does not match ssh config host name, preventing `datalad install` from running correctly.\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\nI am attempting to install across SSH hops.. so my config file looks something like\n```\nHost A.edu\n     User seldamat\n     ForwardAgent yes\n     ServerAliveInterval 240\n     ServerAliveCountMax 2\n     IdentityFile ~/.ssh/rsa\n\nHost B, B-Alias\n    User seldamat\n    ForwardAgent yes\n    ProxyCommand ssh -q A nc  B 22\n    ServerAliveInterval 240\n    ServerAliveCountMax 2\n    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/rsa\n\nHost C, C-Alias\n    User username\n    ForwardAgent yes\n    ProxyCommand ssh -q B-alias nc C 22\n    ServerAliveInterval 240\n    ServerAliveCountMax 2\n```\n\nMy .gitmodule looks like\n```\n[submodule \"dataset\"]\n\tpath = dataset\n\turl = ssh://admin@C-Alias:/home/username/datasets/central-repository/dataset.git\n```\n\nI am running (note that this is being run within a dataset itself)\n`datalad install dataset`\n\nError message is (excerpt):\n```\n[INFO   ] Cloning ssh://admin@C-Alias:/home/username/datasets/central-repository/dataset.git [1 other candidates] into '/gpfs/dataset'\nssh_exchange_identification: Connection closed by remote host\n[WARNING] Failed to run cmd ['ssh', '-fN', '-o', 'ControlMaster=auto', '-o', 'ControlPersist=15m', '-o', 'ControlPath=\"/storage/home/sue217/.cache/datalad/sockets/f7ed4923\"', 'username@c-alias']. Exit code=255\n| stdout: None\n| stderr: None\nssh_exchange_identification: Connection closed by remote host\n[WARNING] Failed to run cmd ['ssh', '-fN', '-o', 'ControlMaster=auto', '-o', 'ControlPersist=15m', '-o', 'ControlPath=\"/storage/home/sue217/.cache/datalad/sockets/f7ed4923\"', 'username@c-alias']. Exit code=255\n| stdout: None\n| stderr: None\n```\n\nI noticed that the host name was incorrectly capitalized so I added this host name to the list\n```\nHost C, C-Alias, c-alias\n    User username\n    ForwardAgent yes\n    ProxyCommand ssh -q B-alias nc C 22\n    ServerAliveInterval 240\n    ServerAliveCountMax 2\n```\n\nAfter this modification \n`datalad install dataset`\n\nWorks like a charm! \n\nOnly issue is that `git annex sync` doesn't work unless you remove the lowercase host entry. No idea why on this one 🤷🏻‍♂️\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (to assess your expertise/prior luck.  We would welcome your testimonial additions to https://github.com/datalad/datalad/wiki/Testimonials as well)","files":null}]}